# Lineage OS Special Project (LOSP) Manifests

Welcome to the **Lineage OS Special Project (LOSP)** — a custom Android distribution based on LineageOS, tailored for performance, aesthetics, and control. This repository contains the manifest files required to initialize and sync the LOSP source tree.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

Follow these steps to set up your local build environment for **LOSP 23.2**.

### 1. Create the Source Directory

```bash
mkdir LOSP-23.2 && cd LOSP-23.2
```

### 2. Install Repo and Initialize the Manifest
```bash
git lfs install
repo init --depth=1 --no-repo-verify -u https://github.com/Lineage-OS-Special-Project/losp_manifests -b crDroid --git-lfs
```

📝 On the first run, this may take some time as it fetches all the required Android source files.

## 🔄 Syncing the Source

Choose the method that suits your connection speed and system stability:
### ✅ Recommended: Optimized Sequential Sync

Stable and reliable, especially on slower or inconsistent connections:
```bash
repo --color=always sync -j1 -cv --force-remove-dirty --optimized-fetch --no-tags --no-clone-bundle --no-repo-verify --fail-fast --prune --force-sync
```

### ⚡ Parallel Sync (Fast Connections Only)

Faster sync for users with strong network performance:
```bash
repo --color=always sync -j$(($(nproc) + 1)) -cv --no-tags --no-clone-bundle --no-repo-verify --fail-fast --optimized-fetch --prune --force-sync
```

## 🧹 Manifest Update Issues

If you encounter an error during `repo sync` after a manifest change (e.g. branch update, repo additions), try resetting the manifest cache:

```bash
rm -rf .repo/manifests/ .repo/manifests.git/
```

Then reinitialize the manifest and re-sync

## 🧱 Building LOSP
1. Set Up the Build Environment
```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
```

### 2. Build an ADB Flashable Image
```bash
m losp -j$(($(nproc) + 1))
```

### 3. Build a Fastboot Flashable Image
```bash
m updatepackage -j$(($(nproc) + 1))
```

## 🙋 Need Help?

If you run into issues, try the following:

- Re-sync using `-j1` to reduce race conditions.
- Clear local manifests:
```bash
rm -rf .repo/local_manifests
```

- Ensure all required build dependencies are installed for your Linux distribution.

More documentation and device setup guides coming soon!

## 🛠️ About LOSP

LOSP is a forward-thinking Android distribution with a focus on:

- Clean performance and system responsiveness
- Feature-rich customization via ModCenter
- Enhanced user control and privacy
- Aesthetic refinements over stock AOSP/Lineage builds

We welcome contributors, testers, and feedback. Stay tuned for future updates!

